5/03/wednesday-assorted-links-493.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=wednesday-assorted-links-493">Wednesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.ft.com/content/d576d67b-760b-49df-ad42-6835795f43fe</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.ft.com/content/d576d67b-760b-49df-ad42-6835795f43fe</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Mar 2025 15:58:52 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Martin Casado on AGI and employment]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1556885485888237568/HH1iBQNp_200x200.jpg"></p><p>martin_casado (@martin_casado) on X</p><p>My rough view on current models and AGI:
- it’s best measured economic value in a productive (not speculative) market
